The class JsonWebHelperHttpClient has a protected readonly HttpClient _httpClient field initialized by constructor injection. The method GetResponseUncheckedAsync calls _httpClient.SendAsync directly, which is non-virtual and cannot be mocked easily. The class does not have an interface or wrapper for HttpClient.

Since the refactor tool is not available, I cannot make the method virtual or inject a wrapper interface. I will write a test that uses a real HttpClient with a mocked HttpMessageHandler to simulate SendAsync behavior. This is a common approach to test code that uses HttpClient.

I will write a test class JsonWebHelperHttpClientTests with a test for GetResponseUncheckedAsync that verifies the call to SendAsync and the returned HttpResponseMessage. I will also test the exception path where SendAsync throws and the AttemptParseAndThrowExceptionAsync is called (I will mock or override that method if possible).

I will submit the test file now.

